{
 "id": "AT-RS-14 (helper part), AT-RS-22, AT-RS-24, AT-RS-41, AT-RS-42 (SESSION-RESTART §2.1-§2.3, B7, R5)",
 "note": "The background route. The gate: the job folder's state.json must name this session (job-unknown); respawnFlags with --dangerously-skip-permissions or --permission-mode bypassPermissions (the = form too) while the fresh mode is not bypass refuse bypass-left, --allow-dangerously-skip-permissions alone passes; a background task or a session cron in the newest Stop slot refuses background-work (with the task types) or crons. respawn sets the carry note sent and starts `claude respawn <short>` detached: the stub claude finds itself in its own process group under a parent that is no child of the helper, with stdin from /dev/null and no CLAUDE_JOB_DIR, CLAUDE_BG_* or $st name in its env; the result file holds rc and the B6 code from its output, the output file is 0600, and a non-zero rc writes one refresh_failed {why: respawn-failed, code} row. respawn-cancel with another nonce kills nothing. A minute later ident reports the after-kill failure once (the note becomes reported), and status prints the claude respawn and claude attach line. respawn reads state.json again: a bypass the mode in respawnFlags has left since the gate (a Shift+Tab during the grace) refuses bypass-left and starts nothing. The detached helper writes its pid record before it answers and reads the note again right before the client runs: a cancel in between leaves the client unrun. respawn-cancel with the nonce settles the note (failed here) and TERMs the group. Two concurrent claims: one winner. B9: respawnFlags holding a flag the restart's sanitizer drops (Claude Code 2.1.312's keep-set; every dropped flag but session selection, -m, --debug and display flags counts, unknown ones included), respawnFlags that are not a list, or none at all, refuse restriction-lost at the gate and again at the respawn; onto a version whose keep-set was not checked (@KEEPSET_CHECKED) a flag whose loss may widen the session (any but the model, effort, name, session id, debug output, the bypass flags and a permission mode other than plan or dontAsk) refuses keepset-unverified. The respawn checks the ship gate (bg-not-shipped) and the setting (off) itself, before anything else. The background route's ship gate: bg-not-shipped without the test seam (the case runs with STORE_TEST_RESTART_BG=1), at the gate and at the arm. Shadow: background work is listed as items, not refused",
 "now": "2026-10-21T14:05:12+03:00",
 "tz": "Etc/GMT-3",
 "options": {"restart_on_update": "on"},
 "env": {"STORE_TEST_RESTART_BG": "1"},
 "steps": [
  {"setup": [
    {"write": "$TMP/jobs/job1/state.json", "json": {"state": "running", "sessionId": "$SID", "respawnFlags": ["--model", "opus", "--dangerously-skip-permissions", "--permission-mode", "default"]}},
    {"write": "$TMP/proj/$SID.jsonl", "content": "{\"type\":\"user\"}\n"},
    {"write": "$HOME/.claude.json", "json": {}},
    {"stub": "claude", "script": "{ echo \"argv=$*\"; env | grep -E '^(CLAUDE_JOB_DIR|CLAUDE_BG_|CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_KIND|CLAUDE_CODE_RESUME_)' ; echo \"self=$$ parent=$PPID\"; ps -o pgid= -p $$ | tr -d ' ' | sed 's/^/pgid=/'; ps -o ppid= -p $PPID | tr -d ' ' | sed 's/^/grandparent=/'; if [ -t 0 ]; then echo stdin=tty; else echo stdin=not-tty; fi; } > \"$STUB_OUT\"; echo 'Error: job_respawn_spawn_failed (cwd_gone)'; exit 1"}
  ]},
  {"name": "(a main Stop with nothing in the background)", "argv": ["hook", "Stop"],
   "stdin_json": {"session_id": "$SID", "transcript_path": "$TMP/proj/$SID.jsonl", "cwd": "$TMP", "hook_event_name": "Stop", "stop_hook_active": false, "permission_mode": "default", "background_tasks": [], "session_crons": []},
   "expect": {"exit": 0}},
  {"name": "(the main PostCompact)", "argv": ["hook", "PostCompact"],
   "stdin_json": {"session_id": "$SID", "transcript_path": "$TMP/proj/$SID.jsonl", "cwd": "$TMP", "hook_event_name": "PostCompact", "trigger": "auto", "permission_mode": "default", "compact_summary": "x"},
   "expect": {"exit": 0}},
  {"name": "a launch bypass left in respawnFlags while the mode is default: bypass-left", "argv": ["restart", "gate", "--sid", "$SID", "--route", "bg", "--job-dir", "$TMP/jobs/job1", "--from", "2.1.311", "--to", "2.1.312"],
   "expect": {"exit": 0, "json": {"ok": false, "why": "bypass-left", "job_short": "job1"}}},
  {"setup": [{"write": "$TMP/jobs/job1/state.json", "json": {"sessionId": "$SID", "respawnFlags": ["--permission-mode=bypassPermissions"]}}]},
  {"name": "the = form too", "argv": ["restart", "gate", "--sid", "$SID", "--route", "bg", "--job-dir", "$TMP/jobs/job1", "--from", "2.1.311", "--to", "2.1.312"],
   "expect": {"exit": 0, "json": {"why": "bypass-left"}}},
  {"setup": [{"write": "$TMP/jobs/job1/state.json", "json": {"sessionId": "$SID", "respawnFlags": ["--allow-dangerously-skip-permissions", "--permission-mode", "default"]}}]},
  {"name": "availability alone is carried: ok", "argv": ["restart", "gate", "--sid", "$SID", "--route", "bg", "--job-dir", "$TMP/jobs/job1", "--from", "2.1.311", "--to", "2.1.312"],
   "expect": {"exit": 0, "json": {"ok": true, "route": "bg", "job_short": "job1", "mode": "default"}}},
  {"setup": [{"write": "$TMP/jobs/job1/state.json", "json": {"sessionId": "$SID", "respawnFlags": ["--tools", "Read", "Grep", "--settings", "/s/settings.json", "--allowedTools", "Bash(git:*)", "--disallowedTools=Write", "--mcp-config", "m.json", "n.json", "--strict-mcp-config", "--add-dir", "/d", "--plugin-dir", "/p", "--system-prompt-file", "/sp", "--setting-sources", "user", "--permission-prompt-tool", "mcp__x__y", "--restricted", "--safe-mode", "--bare", "--disable-slash-commands", "--agents", "{}", "-m", "opus", "-d", "api", "--name", "n", "fix", "the bug", "--permission-mode", "default"]}}]},
  {"name": "B9: every restriction a restart applies again (Claude Code 2.1.312's keep-set), with -m, --debug and prompt words dropped: ok", "argv": ["restart", "gate", "--sid", "$SID", "--route", "bg", "--job-dir", "$TMP/jobs/job1", "--from", "2.1.311", "--to", "2.1.312"], "expect": {"exit": 0, "json": {"ok": true, "route": "bg"}}},
  {"setup": [{"write": "$TMP/jobs/job1/state.json", "json": {"sessionId": "$SID", "respawnFlags": ["--model", "opus", "--frobnicate", "x", "--permission-mode", "default"]}}]},
  {"name": "B9: an unknown flag a restart drops: restriction-lost (it may restrict the session)", "argv": ["restart", "gate", "--sid", "$SID", "--route", "bg", "--job-dir", "$TMP/jobs/job1", "--from", "2.1.311", "--to", "2.1.312"], "expect": {"exit": 0, "json": {"ok": false, "why": "restriction-lost", "job_short": {"null": true}}}},
  {"setup": [{"write": "$TMP/jobs/job1/state.json", "json": {"sessionId": "$SID", "respawnFlags": ["--permission-mode", "default", "--tools"]}}]},
  {"name": "B9: --tools with no value is dropped by the restart: restriction-lost", "argv": ["restart", "gate", "--sid", "$SID", "--route", "bg", "--job-dir", "$TMP/jobs/job1", "--from", "2.1.311", "--to", "2.1.312"], "expect": {"exit": 0, "json": {"why": "restriction-lost"}}},
  {"setup": [{"write": "$TMP/jobs/job1/state.json", "json": {"sessionId": "$SID", "respawnFlags": "--tools Read"}}]},
  {"name": "B9: respawnFlags that are not a list: restriction-lost", "argv": ["restart", "gate", "--sid", "$SID", "--route", "bg", "--job-dir", "$TMP/jobs/job1", "--from", "2.1.311", "--to", "2.1.312"], "expect": {"exit": 0, "json": {"why": "restriction-lost"}}},
  {"setup": [{"write": "$TMP/jobs/job1/state.json", "json": {"sessionId": "$SID"}}]},
  {"name": "B9: no respawnFlags at all (Claude Code reads them as none and respawns with no flag): restriction-lost", "argv": ["restart", "gate", "--sid", "$SID", "--route", "bg", "--job-dir", "$TMP/jobs/job1", "--from", "2.1.311", "--to", "2.1.312"], "expect": {"exit": 0, "json": {"ok": false, "why": "restriction-lost"}}},
  {"setup": [{"write": "$TMP/jobs/job1/state.json", "json": {"sessionId": "$SID", "respawnFlags": ["--model", "opus", "--tools", "Read", "--permission-mode", "default"]}}]},
  {"name": "B9: a restriction 2.1.312 keeps, onto 2.1.312 (a checked keep-set): ok", "argv": ["restart", "gate", "--sid", "$SID", "--route", "bg", "--job-dir", "$TMP/jobs/job1", "--from", "2.1.311", "--to", "2.1.312"], "expect": {"exit": 0, "json": {"ok": true}}},
  {"name": "B9: the same onto 2.1.399 (a keep-set not checked: it may keep less): keepset-unverified", "argv": ["restart", "gate", "--sid", "$SID", "--route", "bg", "--job-dir", "$TMP/jobs/job1", "--from", "2.1.312", "--to", "2.1.399"], "expect": {"exit": 0, "json": {"ok": false, "why": "keepset-unverified", "job_short": {"null": true}}}},
  {"setup": [{"write": "$TMP/jobs/job1/state.json", "json": {"sessionId": "$SID", "respawnFlags": ["--permission-mode=plan"]}}]},
  {"name": "B9: plan onto 2.1.399 (lost, the session would start in default, which is wider): keepset-unverified", "argv": ["restart", "gate", "--sid", "$SID", "--route", "bg", "--job-dir", "$TMP/jobs/job1", "--from", "2.1.312", "--to", "2.1.399"], "expect": {"exit": 0, "json": {"why": "keepset-unverified"}}},
  {"setup": [{"write": "$TMP/jobs/job1/state.json", "json": {"sessionId": "$SID", "respawnFlags": ["--model", "opus", "--effort", "high", "-n", "x", "--session-id", "$SID", "--debug-file", "/d", "--verbose", "--allow-dangerously-skip-permissions", "--permission-mode", "default"]}}]},
  {"name": "B9: onto 2.1.399 with only flags whose loss widens nothing (model, effort, name, session id, debug output, a permission mode not plan or dontAsk): ok", "argv": ["restart", "gate", "--sid", "$SID", "--route", "bg", "--job-dir", "$TMP/jobs/job1", "--from", "2.1.312", "--to", "2.1.399"], "expect": {"exit": 0, "json": {"ok": true, "job_short": "job1"}}},
  {"setup": [{"write": "$TMP/jobs/job1/state.json", "json": {"sessionId": "$SID", "respawnFlags": ["--allow-dangerously-skip-permissions", "--permission-mode", "default"]}}]},
